::ALG1_U02_L02_GP01::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L02_GP01<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>No new primary MLA standard; prerequisite support.<br><br>Question:<br>Solve 3x + 4 = 19. {
= x = 5#Correct. Subtract 4 to get 3x = 15, then divide by 3.
~ x = 7#This divides too early or does not undo both operations in order.
~ x = 15#This stops after subtracting 4 and does not divide by 3.
~ x = 23#This adds 4 instead of subtracting 4.
}

::ALG1_U02_L02_GP02::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L02_GP02<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>No new primary MLA standard; prerequisite support.<br><br>Question:<br>Solve 2m - 7 = 11. {
~ m = 2#This does not undo the subtraction and multiplication correctly.
= m = 9#Correct. Add 7 to get 2m = 18, then divide by 2.
~ m = 18#This stops after adding 7 and does not divide by 2.
~ m = -2#This uses the wrong inverse operation for -7.
}

::ALG1_U02_L02_GP03::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L02_GP03<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>No new primary MLA standard; prerequisite support.<br><br>Question:<br>Solve y/4 + 6 = 10. {
~ y = 1#This divides after subtracting instead of multiplying by 4.
~ y = 4#This stops after subtracting 6 and does not undo division by 4.
= y = 16#Correct. Subtract 6 to get y/4 = 4, then multiply by 4.
~ y = 64#This multiplies before undoing the added 6.
}

::ALG1_U02_L02_GP04::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L02_GP04<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>No new primary MLA standard; prerequisite support.<br><br>Question:<br>Solve -5p - 3 = 17. {
~ p = -14#This subtracts 3 instead of adding 3 first.
~ p = 4#This loses the negative sign after dividing by -5.
~ p = -20#This stops before dividing by -5.
= p = -4#Correct. Add 3 to get -5p = 20, then divide by -5.
}

::ALG1_U02_L02_GP05::
Question ID:<br>ALG1_U02_L02_GP05<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>No new primary MLA standard; prerequisite support.<br><br>Question:<br>A gym charges 8 dollars plus 6 dollars per visit. The total is 38 dollars. How many visits? {
= 5#Correct. 6v + 8 = 38, so 6v = 30 and v = 5.
~ 4#Check: 8 + 6(4) = 32, not 38.
~ 6#Check: 8 + 6(6) = 44, not 38.
~ 30#This stops after subtracting 8 and does not divide by 6.
}
